From: ae-automation-bot <ae-automation-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:34:17 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 133/148] [ae-patch] Stop counting a closed subagent toward its
 parent's waiting badge

A sidebar row's hourglass count (active_child_count, patch 0074) counts a
direct child while the status cache reads running or waiting. Closing a
subagent with sys_session_close archives it, and a child still marked running
when that happened kept the mark: its runner was gone, so no idle edge ever
came, the parent's badge stayed lit for hours and GET /v1/sessions/{id} kept
reading running. Two parts. The session list and the updates stream now ask
list_child_conversation_ids_by_parent for unarchived children only (a new
include_archived keyword, default True, so recovery and the stop sweep still
see every child); the archived flag is on the row that query already reads,
so it costs no extra query and holds on every replica and across restarts.
settle_archived_session in ae_session_activity, called from _archive_stop
after the best-effort stop, publishes idle for a session still marked running
or waiting (the cache, or the stored live_status after a restart), which also
persists the stored status and cancels patch 0125's staleness timer; failed is
left alone.
